(a) In general. No person shall operate a mobile food service unit within the corporate limits of the city without first obtaining the proper licenses and/or permits from the state, county, and the City of Douglas. Mobile food service unit operators shall at all times comply with the provisions of this article and all other applicable local, state, and federal laws, regulations, or rules. All approvals will be issued annually based on the calendar year. No approval issued under this article may be prorated, transferred, assigned, or used by any person other than the one to whom it is issued, or at any location other than the one for which it is issued.
(b) Specific requirements. Any person intending to operate a mobile food service unit within the corporate limits of the City of Douglas shall obtain, prior to commencing operation:
(1) All permits as may be required to operate a food truck and/or mobile food service unit by the state, including the department of public health, and Coffee County, including the health department and/or the Georgia Department of Agriculture;
(2) A City of Douglas mobile food service unit location approval; and
(3) A City of Douglas occupational tax certificate.
(c) Mobile food service unit location approval application—Contents. Applicants seeking mobile food service unit location approval shall submit, on an annual basis, an application for such approval to the city marshal, or his/her designee. Such application shall include:
(1) The name, address, telephone number, and email address of the mobile food service unit's owner(s) of record. An approval shall be required for each mobile food service unit.
(2) Information identifying the mobile service unit including, its make, model and license plate number, together with a photograph of the mobile food service unit;
(3) The corporate and, where applicable, the trade name of the base of operations associated with the mobile food service unit, together with a copy of the base of operation's occupational tax certificate. Where the base of operation is located outside the city limits, the applicant shall provide evidence of licensing in the base of operation's home jurisdiction;
(4) A copy of the approved permit and inspection certificate for the base of operation issued by the Coffee County Public Health Department or Georgia Department of Agriculture;
(5) A listing of operating locations, schedule for operation, and hours of operation for each site on which the mobile food service unit intends to conduct business; written consent or a fully executed copy of the lease agreement for each operating location;
(6) A scaled drawing for each location illustrating the location of the mobile food service unit;
(7) Temporary seating may be provided if the mobile food service unit is at least 1,000 feet from a brick-and-mortar restaurant. A scaled drawing, indicating where the seating will be located and number of seats must be furnished;
(8) Any other information that the city manager or his designee may, from time- to- time, deem material to the approval of mobile food service units within the city limits; and
(9) Application for location approval and renewal shall be accompanied by such fee as established and set by the schedule of fees.
(Ord. No. 03272023, 3-27-2023)

